Scientific inference and preprocessing derive from SynthSR:
Iglesias JE, Billot B, Balbastre Y, et al. (2021).
Joint super-resolution and synthesis of 1 mm isotropic MP-RAGE volumes from
clinical MRI exams with scans of different orientation, resolution and contrast.
NeuroImage 237:118206. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuroimage.2021.118206

Reference: https://github.com/neurolabusc/py_synthsr
Commit: 04ab5548f4609c2b44ca51b3f4bc319b585dafa7
Original: https://github.com/BBillot/SynthSR
The reference utilities include Neurite and Lab2Im contributions, retained here
under the upstream Apache-2.0 license. Model checkpoint: synthsr_v20_230130.h5.

Changes: browser image I/O, JavaScript spatial preprocessing/postprocessing,
ONNX conversion, WebGPU/WASM inference, optional approximate tiled inference,
a Neurodesk/NiiVue interface, and a native Node.js CLI with offline model caching.
No model retraining.
NiiVue and ONNX Runtime retain their respective upstream licenses.
